      "case_index": 20,
      "evidence": [
        "A-E-CAPTURE-078",
        "A-E-COMPLETION-09"
      ],
      "assessment": "ATCC gives KOH pH adjustment but no supplied form, strength, dose or carrier. TOGO separately and explicitly names KOH solusion, labels potassium hydroxide solution and classifies Solution. The solution-qualified local preparation identity is supported only at that TOGO occurrence scope. Neither the trace-table water nor its approximately 500 ml dissolution / final 1 L volume establishes a KOH-stock carrier, concentration or batch volume. The new summary correctly separates these claims. The unchanged single UNMAPPED KOH component and UNKNOWN completeness retain unquantified input without exact solid/hydrate identity, final neutralization-species or pH-as-stock-property claims."
    },
    {
      "case_index": 38,
      "evidence": [
        "A-E-CAPTURE-102"
      ],
      "assessment": "JCM1344 prints 1% Yeast extract solution, 1 ml receiving addition after cooling, under its autoclaved-or-starred-filter-sterilized key. This entry is unstarred, supporting the unchanged separately autoclaved statement. The basal 935 ml water and receiving N2/CO2 atmosphere are not the yeast-stock formulation. New summary preserves strength and dose while correctly leaving stock carrier, product and percent basis unknown. One UNMAPPED Yeast extract component at literal 1 PERCENT, UNKNOWN completeness and no 10 g/L conversion remain supported. No gas, preparation volume, carrier grade, product identity or resolving generic alias is invented."
    }
  ],
